  "intro_html": "<p>Among the many alpine routes on Pilatus the one on the east ridge is certainly the most popular. The itinerary is logical, sneaky, and the difficulties increase, the higher you climb (welcome warm-up phase). Moreover, if necessary, you can leave the ridge on several points. It is an ideal target for those who like challenging itineraries in pre-alpine landscapes.</p>",
